   "evidence": "`finrank \ud835\udd5c F = 1` already makes F finite-dimensional. Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/Module/FiniteDimension.lean:198 `LinearMap.continuous_iff_isClosed_ker` needs only a nontrivially normed field, not completeness. Trivialization.lean:710 `def lineCoord : E b \u2243L[\ud835\udd5c] \ud835\udd5c` is stated for `[FiberBundle \ud835\udd5c E] [VectorBundle \ud835\udd5c \ud835\udd5c E]`, and the new docstring says that for model fibre \ud835\udd5c the new definition is `lineCoord`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/VectorBundle/Trivialization.lean",
   "fix": "Generalise `lineCoord` itself to any model fibre `F` with `hF : finrank \ud835\udd5c F = 1`, without `CompleteSpace` or `FiniteDimensional`: get finite-dimensionality from `hF`, and get continuity of the inverse from its closed kernel `{0}` via `LinearMap.continuous_iff_isClosed_ker`. Use it in `tensorEquivOfNeZero` and drop `lineCoordOfFinrankEqOne`.",
   "issue": "`lineCoordOfFinrankEqOne` assumes `[CompleteSpace \ud835\udd5c]` and `[FiniteDimensional \ud835\udd5c F]`, but neither is needed. It also sits beside `lineCoord` (line 710), its model-fibre-\ud835\udd5c special case, which is not derived from it. So `continuous_lineCoord`, `sectionTrivialization` and the `lineCoord_*` lemmas still cover only model fibre \ud835\udd5c, and when the model fibre is \ud835\udd5c there are two separate definitions of the same coordinate.",
   "line": 839
  }
 ],
